From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giga Edge SDK <noreply@giga-edge-sdk.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] span-tagger: bidirectional Qwen3 encoder with a token
 tagging head

Architecture "span-tagger": the qwen3 backbone weights load as for qwen3.
The graph runs the qwen3 layers with attention without a KV cache
(bidirectional, as for BERT), outputs every token, normalizes the outputs of
the tapped layers (tagger.tap_layers) with a parameter-free layer norm,
concatenates them and applies Linear -> GELU -> Linear. The logits come out
as token embeddings (n_embd_out = number of tags), so the context needs
embeddings = true, pooling NONE and n_ubatch >= n_tokens. The head is not
quantized. The sliding window of the backbone config is ignored: the encoder
attends over the whole text.

test-llama-archs skips the architecture (its dummy model has no tagger
head); test-span-tagger checks that a sliding window key changes nothing.
